additives (HTM/toluene/Li-TFSI solution/t-BP solution $=20\mathrm{mg}/1\mathrm{mL}/15$ $\upmu\upiota$ $.(770\mathrm{mg};7\mathrm{mL})/30$ ${}^{130}\upmu\mathrm{L}$ (1 mL:1 mL)) was drop-casted on the ${\mathsf{M A P b B r}}_{3}/$ $T_{1}0_{2}/\mathsf{F T O}$ substrate and the PCBM/MAPbI3/PEDOT:PSS/ITO substrate was covered on the wet P3HT or $\mathsf{P T A A/M A P b B r_{3}/T i O_{2}/F T O}$ substrate. Then the two substrates were pressurized by double clip (Whasin) as shown in Figure S2 (Supporting Information) and were dried for $4\ h$ under atmosphere. After complete drying of the tandem cell, the double clips were removed for further characterization. All device fabrication procedure was performed below $50\%$ of relative humidity.
Device Characterization: To measure the photovoltaic performance of sandwiched solar cells, the current density–voltage $\left(J-V\right)$ curves were measured by using a solar simulator (Peccell, PEC-L01) with a potentiostat (IVIUM, IviumStat) under illumination of 1 sun ( $\mathsf{l o o m w c m}^{-2}$ AM 1.5G) which was calibrated by Si-reference cell certificated by JIS (Japanese Industrial Standards). For the measurement of J–V hysteresis with respect to the scan direction, the forward and reverse scan rates were set to $10~\mathrm{mV}/200~\mathrm{ms}$ . The $J-V$ curves of all devices were measured by masking the active area with metal mask of $0.096~\mathsf{c m}^{2}$ . The EQE was measured by a power source (ABET 150 W Xenon lamp, 13014) with a monochromator (Dongwoo Optron Co., Ltd., MonoRa-500i) and a potentiostat (IVIUM, IviumStat).
